    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Connect the charger while you apply the fixes. Confirm that the charger works. The battery icon should show that the laptop is charging.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 1: Lower the Brightness and Turn On Battery Saver",
      "body": "A bright display can use a significant amount of power. Lowering the brightness and enabling Battery saver can help extend the time between charges.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 2: Find the Apps Using the Most Power",
      "body": "Windows can show which apps have used the most battery. A demanding app, especially one that continues running in the background, may be responsible…",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 3: Shorten the Screen and Sleep Timers",
      "body": "Your laptop continues to use power while the screen is on. Shorter screen and sleep timers reduce battery use when you are away from the device.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 4: Disable Unnecessary Startup Apps",
      "body": "Startup apps launch when Windows starts. Some continue running even when you are not using them, which can increase battery and memory use.",
      "durationInFrames": 330
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 5: Turn Off Unused Wireless Connections and Syncing",
      "body": "Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and file-syncing services can use power while they run in the background.",
      "durationInFrames": 307
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "kicker": "Code",
      "heading": "Fix 6: Restore the Default Power Schemes",
      "steps": [
        {
          "lang": "text",
          "meta": "",
          "value": "powercfg -restoredefaultschemes",
          "code": "powercfg -restoredefaultschemes",
